[1440.373304, "o", "[10/23/26 11:04:17] INFO     all.holmesgpt.driver - HolmesGPT answer:                                                                       \r\n                             **Investigated components**                                                                                    \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             | Kind | Name | Namespace | Status / Evidence |                                                                \r\n                             |------|------|-----------|-------------------|                                                                \r\n                             | **Pod** | `recommendation-74758c88-8nn94` | `astronomy-shop` | Ready = `True`; container listening on port   \r\n                             8080 (log shows successful handling of `ListRecommendations` calls). |                                         \r\n                             | **Service** | `recommendation` | `astronomy-shop` | ClusterIP = `10.96.61.101`, selector                     \r\n                             `opentelemetry.io/name=recommendation` matches the pod labels. |                                               \r\n                             | **Pod** | `otel-collector-agent-ggftv` / `otel-collector-agent-tdbjs` / `otel-collector-agent-zjjvf` |       \r\n                             `astronomy-shop` | Repeated error logs: <br>```\\nerror kubeletstatsreceiver/... call to /stats/summary endpoint\r\n                             failed\\ntls: failed to verify certificate: x509: cannot validate certificate for 172.18.0.X because it doesn't \r\n                             contain any IP SANs\\n``` |                                                                                     \r\n                             | **Alert** | `ServiceEndpointDown` (deployment = `recommendation`) | `astronomy-shop` | Firing since          \r\n                             `2026‑10‑23T10:54:49Z`; reason: “Service endpoint recommendation.astronomy-shop:8080 is unreachable.” |        \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             **Findings**                                                                                                   \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             * The **recommendation** pod is running, ready, and serving HTTP on port 8080 – no errors in its logs.         \r\n                             * The **recommendation** Service correctly selects the pod (labels match) and has a valid ClusterIP.           \r\n                             * The **only observed failures** are from the OpenTelemetry Collector agents’ **kubeletstatsreceiver**. Every  \r\n                             scrape of the kubelet `/stats/summary` endpoint fails with a TLS verification error because the kubelet’s      \r\n                             serving certificate does **not contain the node’s IP address as a Subject Alternative Name (SAN)**.            \r\n                             * The collector’s failure to scrape kubelet metrics prevents it from exposing node‑level metrics that the      \r\n                             blackbox exporter (or other monitoring components) rely on for health checks. Consequently the                 \r\n                             `ServiceEndpointDown` alert for the recommendation service is triggered even though the service itself is      \r\n"]
[1440.373602, "o", "                             reachable.                                                                                                     \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             **ROOT CAUSE**                                                                                                 \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             * **Faulty component:** `kubeletstatsreceiver` in the OpenTelemetry Collector agents                           \r\n                             (`otel-collector-agent-ggftv`, `otel-collector-agent-tdbjs`, `otel-collector-agent-zjjvf`).                    \r\n                             * **Root cause:** kubelet TLS certificates lack the node IP in the SAN field, causing TLS verification to fail \r\n                             for the collector’s HTTPS request to `https://<node‑IP>:10250/stats/summary`. The collector logs the error     \r\n                             repeatedly, leading to missing metrics and a downstream alert that the recommendation service endpoint is      \r\n                             unreachable.                                                                                                   \r\n                             * **Evidence:** Repeated error log lines (see collector logs) showing `tls: failed to verify certificate … does\r\n                             not contain any IP SANs`; the alert `ServiceEndpointDown` is firing for the recommendation service despite the \r\n                             pod being ready.                                                                                               \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             **Remediation**                                                                                                \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             1. **Regenerate kubelet certificates** to include the node’s IP address as an IP SAN (or use a SAN‑compatible  \r\n                             wildcard DNS name).                                                                                            \r\n                             2. **Alternatively**, adjust the OpenTelemetry Collector configuration for `kubeletstatsreceiver` to skip TLS  \r\n                             verification (`insecure_skip_verify: true`) if certificate regeneration is not immediately possible.           \r\n                             3. After fixing the certificate or collector config, verify that the collector logs no longer contain the TLS  \r\n                             error and that the `ServiceEndpointDown` alert clears.                                                         \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             All other application pods and services are healthy; the incident is isolated to the collector’s inability to  \r\n                             scrape kubelet metrics due to the TLS SAN misconfiguration.                                                    \r\n"]
